      "question": {
        ":question/id": "77fe6685-0db5-512c-a146-7a7385d90d5f",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}(xy),$ express $f_x(2,3)$ as the limit of a difference quotient.",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "c0a173b9-7073-5910-96e4-56dae5d5791d",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "3882cc29-e493-5280-8251-94acc6ea11be",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\lim_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3+h)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h})"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "cc0c1ad0-0809-5caa-abd0-3c394f9b2ffc",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\lim_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3+h)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h})"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "142263e2-ffc1-5971-aab7-a78e8fb89d3d",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\lim_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h})"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "d6d16f5b-c575-532b-8e3a-633aa682efa9",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\lim_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))}{h})"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "6b6269b9-5085-5358-b7f7-9136abf836c0",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\lim_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))+(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h})"
              }
            ],
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "142263e2-ffc1-5971-aab7-a78e8fb89d3d"
            ]
          }
        ],
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is given by the limit\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{f(2+h, 3)-f(2,3)}{h}).\n$$\n\nSince $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}(xy),$ we have that\n\n$$\nf(2+h, 3)=\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)),\\qquad f(2,3)=\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf_x(2,3)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}(\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}((2+h)(3)))-(\\operatorname{sin}((2)(3)))}{h}).\n$$\n\nHere $h\\ne 0$ before taking the limit, and $y=3$ is held constant."
      },
